{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1119541-guardians-of-the-veil-crossover-question","id":1119541,"title":"Guardians of the Veil crossover question","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-07-23T09:24:19-07:00","id":1119541,"title":"Guardians of the Veil crossover question","content":"Guardians of the Veil---at least in 1e!---are fond of creating fake occultist societies, in an attempt to obfuscate the Truth and shield mages from the Lie. My question is simple: what, in your opinions, would be the Guardians of the Veil's reaction to, say, an Azoth-wielding alchemist joining such a false front?<br /> <br /> Clearly, the alchemist possesses genuine magics...but NOT Supernal magics! Would they observe him, maintaining their masquerade (pardon the pun)? Would they eliminate him?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-23T10:22:20-07:00","id":1119559,"title":"","content":"This tradition of creating Labyrinths to weed out the weak of will and foul of spirit is alive and well amongst the Guardians in 2nd Edition, and to answer your question: yes. <br /> <br /> The Alchemist practices a form of Fallen World magic that hints at the sublime process of both Stygia and the Aether, but is tainted with the Lie. The Guardians would most likely observe this individual, learn what they can about their strange alchemies, and then depending on several factors relating to the Guardian's beliefs and traditions they'll decide whether to start dropping clues to a highter truth beyond the Alchemist's base art or they'll continue to feed their Fallen beliefs in the hope that it will forever trap them in the Lie and keep true magic out of their dangerous hands.<br /> <br /> In the case of an antagonist Alchemist from Promethean, I'd imagine the Guardians would lean more towards the latter once they see that their drive to learn is more about transcending mortal weakness without any negative consiquences rather than spiritual enlightenment. However, each Guardian is their own individual with their own take on the exoteric &amp; esoteric tenets. Which means ultimately their decision is up to you. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-23T15:21:20-07:00","id":1119642,"title":"","content":"IMO, the Guardians are specifically concerned about phenomena like Dissonance and Paradox erasing Supernal magic from the world. They might be thrilled to find a practitioner of vernacular &quot;this world&quot; magic in the Labyrinth, creating a spiritual dead end for seekers who would be satisfied with the base lead of immortality and creating life, rather than escaping the Fallen World.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-24T04:15:31-07:00","id":1119834,"title":"","content":"I don't think the origin matters. The Guardians want their Labyrinths to be almost totally free of the supernatural. Their core aim isn't just protecting magic, they're also protecting the souls of the sleepers. 2e introduced the mechanic that the supernatural causes breaking points, that is, it weakens the souls of sleepers, and Alchemy is particularly bad for sleepers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}